IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `whs-worker`
IMPORT `whs-seat-pcbu`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 -- worked cases, from the seat of the person conducting the business or undertaking.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2024C00243), never copied from the encoding's output. Every case is HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Northline Logistics Pty Ltd (HYPOTHETICAL), a non-Commonwealth licensee still in its transitional period, runs the
-- warehouse where Priya's forklift incident happened (whs-cases-worker.l4), and manages it. MIRROR cases ask the same
-- facts as the worker's case file, from this seat; the answers must agree.

§ `cases`

§§ `s 38`

-- MIRROR (worker: `Is it a notifiable incident` ... in-patient ... TRUE): Priya is admitted to hospital: notify at once.
#ASSERT `Must I notify Comcare` `someone needed immediate treatment as a hospital in-patient` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I must ensure Comcare is notified immediately after I become aware of it, by the fastest possible means, by telephone or in writing, and in writing within 48 hours if Comcare asks (s 38(1) to (4)); I must keep a record of it for at least 5 years (s 38(7))`
-- MIRROR (worker: the falling load that hits nobody): a dangerous incident, notify.
#ASSERT `Must I notify Comcare` `someone was exposed to a serious risk from an immediate or imminent uncontrolled escape, spill, fire, explosion, gas or steam leak, electric shock, fall from height, collapse or failure listed in s 37` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I must ensure Comcare is notified immediately after I become aware of it, by the fastest possible means, by telephone or in writing, and in writing within 48 hours if Comcare asks (s 38(1) to (4)); I must keep a record of it for at least 5 years (s 38(7))`
-- MIRROR (worker: the sprained wrist): no notice.
#ASSERT `Must I notify Comcare` `another injury, illness or incident` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: it is not a notifiable incident arising out of my business or undertaking`
-- MIRROR (worker: the visitor's heart attack): no notice.
#ASSERT `Must I notify Comcare` `someone died` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is not a notifiable incident arising out of my business or undertaking`

-- Notified by telephone on 2 March 2026: keep the record until 2 March 2031.
#ASSERT `Until when must I keep the incident record` (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS Date 2 3 2031
-- Notified on 29 February 2028: until 28 February 2033.
#ASSERT `Until when must I keep the incident record` (Date 29 2 2028) EQUALS Date 28 2 2033

§§ `s 39`

#ASSERT `May the incident site be disturbed` TRUE FALSE `assisting an injured person` EQUALS `yes: s 39(3) allows this action`
#ASSERT `May the incident site be disturbed` TRUE FALSE `what is essential to make the site safe or minimise the risk of a further notifiable incident` EQUALS `yes: s 39(3) allows this action`
-- Clearing the fallen pallet to reopen the aisle before an inspector comes: no.
#ASSERT `May the incident site be disturbed` TRUE FALSE `anything else, such as cleaning up or resuming work` EQUALS `no: I must ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, that the site is not disturbed until an inspector arrives or directs otherwise (s 39(1))`
#ASSERT `May the incident site be disturbed` TRUE TRUE `anything else, such as cleaning up or resuming work` EQUALS `yes: an inspector has arrived, or directed that the site may be disturbed`
-- A labour hire firm whose worker was hurt, but which does not manage or control the warehouse.
#ASSERT `May the incident site be disturbed` FALSE FALSE `anything else, such as cleaning up or resuming work` EQUALS `s 39 does not bind me: I do not manage or control the workplace`

§§ `ss 47 to 49`

-- MIRROR (worker: the new picking system, directly affected, with an HSR).
#ASSERT `Must I consult my workers` `proposing changes that may affect workers' health or safety` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I must consult them, and their health and safety representative must be involved (ss 47, 48(2)); penalty tier C`
-- MIRROR (worker: hazard identification, no HSR).
#ASSERT `Must I consult my workers` `identifying hazards or assessing risks from the work` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must consult them, so far as is reasonably practicable: share the information, let them give their views and contribute, take the views into account and tell them the outcome (ss 47, 48(1)); penalty tier C`
-- MIRROR (worker: not directly affected).
#ASSERT `Must I consult my workers` `proposing changes that may affect workers' health or safety` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 49 does not list this matter, or these workers are not directly affected by it`

§§ `s 87`

-- Priya refused the aisle under s 84; packing orders in the next building is safe and suitable: Northline may direct it.
-- MIRROR (worker: `Is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE FALSE -- she does the packing, continuity protected).
#ASSERT `May I direct alternative work` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May I direct alternative work` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May I direct alternative work` FALSE TRUE

§§ `ss 30A to 33, Schedule 4`

-- Northline, a body corporate (column 4): category 1 $15,000,000; category 2 $2,090,000; category 3 $700,000; industrial
-- manslaughter $18,000,000 (s 30A).
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 15000000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 2090000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 700000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined` `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 18000000, 0)
-- Its warehouse director, an officer (column 2): category 1 $3,000,000 or 15 years; category 3 $140,000; industrial
-- manslaughter 25 years.
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` FALSE EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 3000000, 15)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` FALSE EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 140000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined` `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)` FALSE EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 0, 25)
